Third-party components and data sources
- The Python core uses only the Python standard library. No third-party code is bundled.
- Optional: PyMuPDF 1.28.2 (AGPL-3.0 / commercial licence), pinned and hash-checked in requirements-ocr.txt and installed by Setup into a
  private .venv only if you say yes, and Tesseract OCR (Apache-2.0, installed separately), used only by ocr_run.py. Their licences apply to
  your use of them; neither is distributed with this product.
- Optional, installed separately: the Patent Research Hub (published by Brightline IP), which provides access to
  USPTO Open Data Portal, PTAB and GovInfo APIs. You use your own credentials and are bound by each provider's
  terms of use and rate limits.
- pg_tool/data/uspto_event_codes.csv is the USPTO PatEx 2022 event-code list (event_codes.csv, from https://data.uspto.gov/ui/datasets/products/files/ECOPAIR/2022/event_codes.csv.zip,
  retrieved 2026-11-21 (UTC); SHA-256 of the zip d3dc72afcd38a0e677f116faf979179ec34e0dbc0520e5f9e95c39091ba85c57). USPTO data is in the public domain. Patent Genius's
  mapping of codes to roles (interview, abandonment, ...) is its own.
- Data you download (USPTO file wrappers, PTAB decisions, Federal Circuit opinions via GovInfo, CPC scheme files)
  remains subject to its publisher's terms. No such data is included in this repository.
- tests/fixtures and examples contain only synthetic, invented material.
